# NEVER commit private keys. The CA key can mint a certificate for any member,
# which is a peer credential -- and a Raft peer can propose and commit entries.
# Keys live on the members at /usr/local/etc/etcd/pki/ and in the encrypted
# estate bundle (/etc/secrets.enc). Certificates are public and ARE tracked, so
# the deployment is auditable without exposing anything.
*.key
*.srl
